Yes. This follows directly from the transitive property: if all bloops are razzies**s** (A⊆B), and all razzies are lazzies (B⊆C), then all bloops are lazzies (A⊆C). This is a valid syllogism in logic, specifically a Barbara (AAA-1) syllogism, where both premises are universal affirmatives and the conclusion is a universal affirmative relating the major to the minor term, with the middle term (razzies) being the subject in the major premise and the predicate in the minor premise. In set-theoret
